From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hauke Mehrtens <hauke@hauke-m.de>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: Propagate probe deferral from dedicated drivers

When a dedicated PHY driver matches a PHY device but its probe returns
-EPROBE_DEFER (e.g. firmware not yet available), phylib must NOT fall
back to the generic genphy driver.  Doing so would permanently cripple
the PHY: the genphy driver binds, and when the real driver module loads
later it cannot take over (the device already has a driver).

Add a probe_deferred bit to struct phy_device that records whether the
last dedicated-driver probe returned -EPROBE_DEFER.  In
phy_attach_direct(), if no driver is bound and probe_deferred is set,
return -EPROBE_DEFER instead of falling back to genphy.

--- a/drivers/net/phy/phy_device.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/phy_device.c
@@ -1797,6 +1797,16 @@ int phy_attach_direct(struct net_device
 	 * exist, and we should use the genphy driver.
 	 */
 	if (!d->driver) {
+		/* Unless a dedicated driver did match this PHY, but asked to
+		 * be probed again later, e.g. because its firmware is not
+		 * available yet. Papering over that with the generic driver
+		 * would permanently cripple the PHY, so tell the caller to
+		 * come back later as well.
+		 */
+		if (phydev->probe_deferred) {
+			err = -EPROBE_DEFER;
+			goto error_put_device;
+		}
 		if (phydev->is_c45)
 			d->driver = &genphy_c45_driver.mdiodrv.driver;
 		else
@@ -3547,6 +3557,7 @@ static int phy_probe(struct device *dev)
 	int err = 0;
 
 	phydev->drv = phydrv;
+	phydev->probe_deferred = 0;
 
 	/* Disable the interrupt if the PHY doesn't support it
 	 * but the interrupt is still a valid one
@@ -3664,6 +3675,10 @@ static int phy_probe(struct device *dev)
 	return 0;
 
 out:
+	/* Remember that a dedicated driver wants to be probed again later, so
+	 * that phy_attach_direct() does not bind the generic driver instead.
+	 */
+	phydev->probe_deferred = (err == -EPROBE_DEFER);
 	sfp_bus_del_upstream(phydev->sfp_bus);
 	phydev->sfp_bus = NULL;
 
--- a/include/linux/phy.h
+++ b/include/linux/phy.h
@@ -661,6 +661,7 @@ struct phy_device {
 	unsigned mac_managed_pm:1;
 	unsigned wol_enabled:1;
 	unsigned is_genphy_driven:1;
+	unsigned probe_deferred:1;
 
 	unsigned autoneg:1;
 	/* The most recently read link state */
